==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From obsolete {{etyl|fr|en}} {{term|prominence|lang=fr}} (compare {{term|proéminence|lang=fr}}), from {{etyl|la|en}} {{lena}} {{term|prominentia|lang=la}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|prominences}}

#The state of being [[prominent]]: widely known or [[eminent]].
#*{{RQ:Frgsn Zlnstn|IV}}
#*:“My Continental '''prominence''' is improving,” I commented dryly. ¶ Von Lindowe cut at a furze bush with his silver-mounted rattan. ¶ “Quite so,” he said as dryly, his hand at his mustache. “I may say if your intentions were known your life would not be worth a curse.”
#[[relative|Relative]] [[importance]].
#A [[bulge]]: something that bulges out or is [[protuberant]] or [[project]]s from a form.
#{{lb|en|topography}} Autonomous height; relative height or prime factor; a concept used in the categorization of [[hill]]s and [[mountain]]s.

